WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.040
Responsible AI red teaming begins with clear scope and authorization.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:14.340
Teams should define what systems are in scope, what risks are being tested, what data may be used, what actions are prohibited, who must be notified, and how findings will be handled.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.520
Scope protects people, data, and systems.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:26.220
Testing should avoid unnecessary production disruption, avoid exposing sensitive data, and respect legal, contractual, and organizational boundaries.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.640
Safety is part of the assessment design, not an afterthought.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.900
Rules of engagement should also define stop conditions.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:43.360
If testing reveals unexpected impact, sensitive exposure, unstable behavior, or unclear authorization, the team should know when to pause and who to contact.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.980
Clear boundaries make findings more credible.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:52.840
They also help testers focus on the agreed risk questions instead of drifting into activities that do not support the assessment objective.
